 "text": "These farms run on water from the last Ice Age.\n\nIn 1987, this was empty desert.\n\nThen the circles came.\n\nEach is a farm about a kilometer wide, watered by a rotating sprinkler arm.\n\nBy 1992, the desert kingdom was exporting over two million tons of wheat.\n\nThe water is pumped from deep aquifers filled about twenty thousand years ago.\n\nRain here can't refill them.\n\nIn 2016, Saudi Arabia ended its wheat program to save water.\n\nMany farmers switched to alfalfa, which uses three times the water.\n\nThat year, hydrologists estimated about fifty more years of pumping. All of this, built on water that doesn't come back.",
